{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38137578",
      "title": "Defining a First Effect",
      "lectureOrder": 700,
      "videoOrder": 645,
      "sourceHash": "56a49b36085f6ca410e27b61fcc9ed7cbd39864e82ef2fda032552eeccafd65d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 3.66,
          "en": "So here to store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.66,
          "end": 7.62,
          "en": "the counter value whenever it changes in localStorage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.62,
          "end": 10.05,
          "en": "I'll add a new file in my store folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.05,
          "end": 14.103,
          "en": "and I'll name it counter.effects.ts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.21,
          "end": 16.95,
          "en": "Now like all these files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.95,
          "end": 18.78,
          "en": "it's not technically required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.78,
          "end": 21.6,
          "en": "to have that file or to name it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.6,
          "end": 23.52,
          "en": "but it is a good practice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.52,
          "end": 25.92,
          "en": "to have your actions in a separate file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.92,
          "end": 27.99,
          "en": "your reducer in a separate file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.99,
          "end": 29.94,
          "en": "your selectors in a separate file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.94,
          "end": 32.253,
          "en": "and your effects in a separate file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.24,
          "end": 36.24,
          "en": "So here we have the counter.effects.ts file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.24,
          "end": 40.35,
          "en": "and in there we can now create a new effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.35,
          "end": 42.81,
          "en": "and store the logic that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.81,
          "end": 47.16,
          "en": "when a certain action occurs by creating a new class here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.16,
          "end": 48.813,
          "en": "And I'll name it CounterEffects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.03,
          "end": 54.63,
          "en": "Now this class can then contain multiple properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.63,
          "end": 59.37,
          "en": "and every property in the end defines one pipeline,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.37,
          "end": 64.11,
          "en": "you could say, that should be executed for certain actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.11,
          "end": 68.16,
          "en": "So here we could start by adding a saveCount property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.16,
          "end": 69.96000000000001,
          "en": "to the CounterEffects class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.96000000000001,
          "end": 72.93,
          "en": "and the value will be the code pipeline",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.93,
          "end": 74.43,
          "en": "that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.43,
          "end": 77.7,
          "en": "whenever we want a saved account to local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.7,
          "end": 81.18299999999999,
          "en": "so whenever we increment it or decrement it to counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.28999999999999,
          "end": 85.98,
          "en": "For this, we should use the createEffect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.98,
          "end": 89.46000000000001,
          "en": "which must be imported from ngrx/effects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.46000000000001,
          "end": 92.643,
          "en": "so which is coming from this new package we installed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.05,
          "end": 97.74000000000001,
          "en": "CreateEffect creates such an effect value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.74000000000001,
          "end": 100.28999999999999,
          "en": "which should be stored for this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.28999999999999,
          "end": 103.2,
          "en": "And createEffect then actually wants",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.2,
          "end": 105.36,
          "en": "a function as an input value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.36,
          "end": 108.47999999999999,
          "en": "So to the createEffect function which we're executing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.47999999999999,
          "end": 112.17,
          "en": "we're passing a new anonymous function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.17,
          "end": 116.49000000000001,
          "en": "And this function here then should return a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.49000000000001,
          "end": 118.05,
          "en": "that is based on something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.05,
          "end": 120.81,
          "en": "we have to inject into this class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.81,
          "end": 122.61,
          "en": "Therefore, before continuing here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.61,
          "end": 124.41,
          "en": "we can add the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.41,
          "end": 127.68,
          "en": "to use Angular's dependency injection mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.68,
          "end": 131.04,
          "en": "to inject something into this CounterEffects class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.04,
          "end": 133.77,
          "en": "And that something I want to inject in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.77,
          "end": 138.77,
          "en": "is an actions property, which is of type Actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.31,
          "end": 142.41,
          "en": "So not Action but Actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.41,
          "end": 145.113,
          "en": "which is imported from ngrx/effects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.82,
          "end": 150.57,
          "en": "Now actually, Actions here yields an observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.57,
          "end": 153.15,
          "en": "and therefore we can add a dollar sign here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.15,
          "end": 155.13,
          "en": "which is again not technically required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.13,
          "end": 157.56,
          "en": "but often used to make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.56,
          "end": 160.44,
          "en": "that this value here holds an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.44,
          "end": 162.45,
          "en": "and this Actions type under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.45,
          "end": 166.05,
          "en": "does indeed give us such an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.05,
          "end": 169.17000000000002,
          "en": "So we must inject our actions here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.17000000000002,
          "end": 170.91,
          "en": "and now we can use this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.91,
          "end": 172.65,
          "en": "inside of this anonymous function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.65,
          "end": 174.3,
          "en": "and that's why we should also use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.3,
          "end": 176.07,
          "en": "an arrow function here to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 176.07,
          "end": 178.77,
          "en": "that the this keyword when used here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.77,
          "end": 180.48,
          "en": "does refer to this class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.48,
          "end": 183.42,
          "en": "and has access to the injected actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.42,
          "end": 184.71,
          "en": "because we now want to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 184.71,
          "end": 188.04,
          "en": "the injected actions observable here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.04,
          "end": 191.193,
          "en": "to then call pipe on that observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.09,
          "end": 193.89,
          "en": "because that's how you can then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 193.89,
          "end": 198.24,
          "en": "combine different operations based on one observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.24,
          "end": 199.86,
          "en": "when using RxJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 199.86,
          "end": 202.53,
          "en": "And of course, observables are provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 202.53,
          "end": 204.57,
          "en": "by that RxJS library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 204.57,
          "end": 206.94,
          "en": "so we have to use pipe here to then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 206.94,
          "end": 210.9,
          "en": "perform different actions for a this observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 210.9,
          "end": 212.94,
          "en": "And this might still be a bit abstract here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 212.94,
          "end": 215.94,
          "en": "but it will make more sense in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 215.94,
          "end": 219.03,
          "en": "Because now the first action we wanna pipe here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 219.03,
          "end": 221.91,
          "en": "is the ofType action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 221.91,
          "end": 225.78,
          "en": "which must also be imported from ngrx/effects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 225.78,
          "end": 227.57999999999998,
          "en": "And ofType can only be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 227.57999999999998,
          "end": 230.76,
          "en": "inside of such a pipe method call here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 230.76,
          "end": 234.39,
          "en": "Now ofType now simply allows us to define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 234.39,
          "end": 238.47,
          "en": "for which actions we want to continue in this pipe here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 238.47,
          "end": 241.2,
          "en": "and for which actions we want to execute some code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 241.2,
          "end": 244.17,
          "en": "Because what this.actions here is observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 244.17,
          "end": 248.58,
          "en": "in the end does is it yields us a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 248.58,
          "end": 251.43,
          "en": "which we can handle whenever",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 251.43,
          "end": 256.38,
          "en": "anywhere in our application an NgRx action is dispatched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 256.38,
          "end": 259.68,
          "en": "That's what this injected actions object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 259.68,
          "end": 262.26,
          "en": "this.actions observable gives us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 262.26,
          "end": 266.49,
          "en": "It emits a new value whenever anywhere in the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 266.49,
          "end": 268.71,
          "en": "an action is dispatched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 268.71,
          "end": 270.9,
          "en": "And with this ofType operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 270.9,
          "end": 274.92,
          "en": "we can now basically filter those dispatched actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 274.92,
          "end": 277.14,
          "en": "and decide for which actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 277.14,
          "end": 279.96,
          "en": "we want to continue in this pipeline.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 279.96,
          "end": 282.3,
          "en": "For that, ofType then simply takes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 282.3,
          "end": 286.05,
          "en": "these action identifiers as inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 286.05,
          "end": 288.72,
          "en": "For example, here, increment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 288.72,
          "end": 293.25,
          "en": "we can import increment from counter.actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 293.25,
          "end": 295.77,
          "en": "And with that we would now only continue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 295.77,
          "end": 297.69,
          "en": "with the next step in this pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 297.69,
          "end": 299.79,
          "en": "which we'll define in just a second",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 299.79,
          "end": 304.14,
          "en": "if the dispatched action was the increment action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 304.14,
          "end": 307.14,
          "en": "You can also pass more than one value to ofType",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 307.14,
          "end": 309.21,
          "en": "to listen to multiple actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 309.21,
          "end": 312.6,
          "en": "for example, also to the decrement action here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 312.6,
          "end": 314.103,
          "en": "which also must be imported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 315.09,
          "end": 318.06,
          "en": "And you can by the way also not just pass these",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 318.06,
          "end": 321.39300000000003,
          "en": "action functions that are created by using createAction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 322.23,
          "end": 325.2,
          "en": "But instead, if you would be using this alternative syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 325.2,
          "end": 328.77,
          "en": "you can also just pass the action identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 328.77,
          "end": 332.973,
          "en": "either like this or by using a globally available constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 334.2,
          "end": 336.69,
          "en": "Now here I'll go back to using increment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 336.69,
          "end": 338.7,
          "en": "and decrement like this though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 338.7,
          "end": 340.8,
          "en": "But of course, that's not all I want to do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 340.8,
          "end": 343.86,
          "en": "Instead, filtering for certain actions is nice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 343.86,
          "end": 347.04,
          "en": "but we now also wanna define what should happen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 347.04,
          "end": 349.47,
          "en": "when these actions occur.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 349.47,
          "end": 352.32,
          "en": "And here you now got two main options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 352.32,
          "end": 354.93,
          "en": "You can either execute some code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 354.93,
          "end": 358.56,
          "en": "which then should lead to another action being dispatched,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 358.56,
          "end": 361.86,
          "en": "which then should maybe trigger some reducer function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 361.86,
          "end": 363.93,
          "en": "That could make sense if you're, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 363.93,
          "end": 366.57,
          "en": "sending a get request to some backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 366.57,
          "end": 368.58,
          "en": "and you're fetching some data from there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 368.58,
          "end": 371.13,
          "en": "which you then want to use once it's available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 371.13,
          "end": 374.37,
          "en": "to update some data with help of a reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 374.37,
          "end": 376.863,
          "en": "and I'll come back to this use case later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 377.91,
          "end": 380.97,
          "en": "Alternatively, you could also have a pipeline",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 380.97,
          "end": 383.28,
          "en": "that should perform a side effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 383.28,
          "end": 386.1,
          "en": "but not dispatch any other action thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 386.1,
          "end": 388.17,
          "en": "So which shouldn't in the end not trigger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 388.17,
          "end": 391.53,
          "en": "any other side effects or lead to any state changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 391.53,
          "end": 393.6,
          "en": "by reducer functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 393.6,
          "end": 396.24,
          "en": "And that's what I want to do here for this use case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 396.24,
          "end": 399.63,
          "en": "where I want to save some count to the local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 399.63,
          "end": 403.65,
          "en": "Here we can use the tap operator offered by RxJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 403.65,
          "end": 407.61,
          "en": "and therefore you must import it from RxJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 407.61,
          "end": 410.85,
          "en": "And the tap operator allows you to register a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 410.85,
          "end": 414.36,
          "en": "that will be executed that does then not yield",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 414.36,
          "end": 416.49,
          "en": "a new observable once it's done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 416.49,
          "end": 419.1,
          "en": "or that does not yield a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 419.1,
          "end": 420.933,
          "en": "once it's done to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 421.86,
          "end": 424.68,
          "en": "Here inside of tap, we will get the action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 424.68,
          "end": 426.603,
          "en": "that was dispatched as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 427.95,
          "end": 429.39,
          "en": "and then here we could, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 429.39,
          "end": 431.73,
          "en": "console.log that action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 431.73,
          "end": 434.37,
          "en": "and we could also reach out to localStorage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 434.37,
          "end": 437.94,
          "en": "and for example, set a new item here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 437.94,
          "end": 439.95,
          "en": "and the item could be called count,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 439.95,
          "end": 443.1,
          "en": "and the value could be the count which you wanna store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 443.1,
          "end": 445.23,
          "en": "for example, one or two or three,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 445.23,
          "end": 446.52,
          "en": "as a string though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 446.52,
          "end": 448.593,
          "en": "Storing numbers like this is not allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 450.03,
          "end": 452.37,
          "en": "So here we could store the action.value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 452.37,
          "end": 455.31,
          "en": "though that will actually not be the current count,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 455.31,
          "end": 458.1,
          "en": "but just the value by which the count changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 458.1,
          "end": 460.5,
          "en": "Nonetheless, that's what I'll use for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 460.5,
          "end": 462.65999999999997,
          "en": "Here we should just call toString then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 462.65999999999997,
          "end": 464.58,
          "en": "to make sure that this is a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 464.58,
          "end": 467.433,
          "en": "because setItem wants a string value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 468.87,
          "end": 471.9,
          "en": "And with that we would have this action to find.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 471.9,
          "end": 475.26,
          "en": "However, if you have an action pipeline like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 475.26,
          "end": 479.07,
          "en": "which does in the end not dispatch a new action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 479.07,
          "end": 483.51,
          "en": "you should also add a second argument to createEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 483.51,
          "end": 486.63,
          "en": "after this first argument, which is this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 486.63,
          "end": 489.87,
          "en": "And this second argument is a configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 489.87,
          "end": 494.1,
          "en": "where you should set the dispatch property to false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 494.1,
          "end": 496.2,
          "en": "making it clear that this effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 496.2,
          "end": 499.803,
          "en": "does not dispatch a new action once it's done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 500.76,
          "end": 502.2,
          "en": "And you have to set this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 502.2,
          "end": 504.09,
          "en": "because the default indeed is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 504.09,
          "end": 508.23,
          "en": "that effects do dispatch new actions once they are done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 508.23,
          "end": 511.263,
          "en": "And again, you will see this in a couple of minutes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 512.49,
          "end": 514.59,
          "en": "But here I don't wanna dispatch anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 514.59,
          "end": 518.043,
          "en": "and with that, we defined our first side effect.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
